@startuml
' REVIEWED_MAIN_2026_05_13: aligned to current merged code; large-investment retained pending simplification merge.

title Investor Gateway — Attestation Flow (Threat Model View)

' skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
' skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
' skinparam wrapWidth 260
' skinparam sequenceGroupBorderColor #666666
' skinparam noteBorderColor #CC6600
' skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFF3E0
' skinparam sequenceDividerBorderColor #333333
' skinparam sequenceDividerBackgroundColor #E8E8E8

actor "Investor\n(Browser / Wallet)" as Investor
participant "Upstream\nAPI Gateway / WAF" as WAF #LightGray
box "Investor Gateway (trusted zone)" #e0F4eF
  participant "Ktor HTTP\nRouting" as Ktor
  participant "Compliance\nAttestation Signer" as Signer
actor "Vault Admin" as Admin
database "Secret Manager\n(KMS / Vault)" as SM #Wheat
end box
participant "Hypernative\nMonitor (SaaS)" as HN #LightGray
participant "Solana\nVault Program" as Vault #LightSalmon

== INITIALISATION — Keypair Provisioning & On-Chain Registration ==

note over SM #FFE0E0
  **KEYPAIR_SECRET_MANAGER**
  Keypair stored in managed secret store
  with IAM access control, audit logging,
  encryption at rest, rotation support.
end note

Admin -> SM : Generate or import Ed25519 keypair
activate SM
SM --> Admin : Keypair stored\nPublic key returned
deactivate SM

Admin -> Vault : set_compliance_authority(\n  vault, new_pubkey )
activate Vault

note over Admin, Vault
  **Trust anchor binding**
  vault.compliance_authority = signer pubkey.
  Only attestations signed by this key will
  be accepted. Requires vault admin authority.
end note

Vault -> Vault : require signer == vault.admin
Vault -> Vault : vault.compliance_authority\n  := new_pubkey
Vault --> Admin : Tx success
deactivate Vault

note over Admin, Vault #FFCCCC
  **COMPLIANCE_AUTHORITY_ROTATION**
  On suspected compromise: rotate keypair
  in Secret Manager + update on-chain
  compliance_authority atomically.
  Only mechanism to invalidate leaked keys.
end note

== BOOT — Secret Loading & Self-Test ==

note over SM, Signer #FFCCCC
  **SIGNER_KEYPAIR_COMPROMISE**
  Keypair provisioned from Secret Manager
  into env var GATEWAY_ATTESTATION_SIGNER_KEYPAIR.
  Compromise → unlimited forgery of
  compliance attestations.
end note

SM -> Signer : Inject Ed25519 keypair\nvia env var at deploy time
' activate Signer
' Signer -> Signer : Parse 64-byte Solana keypair\n(JSON array or base64)
' Signer -> Signer : keypairIsConsistent()\nSign fixed challenge → verify\nagainst embedded pubkey
' alt Mismatch
'   Signer ->x Signer : **FAIL STARTUP**\nCorrupted or malformed keypair
' else Consistent
'   Signer --> Signer : Boot OK — signer ready
' end
' deactivate Signer

' note over Ktor #FFCCCC
'   **PERMISSIVE_CORS_EXPOSURE**
'   CORS: anyHost() allows any
'   origin to call attestation
'   endpoints from a malicious page.
' end note

SM -> Ktor : Inject Hypernative credentials\n(client-id, secret, bearer)\nvia env vars at deploy time
' Ktor -> Ktor : Configure CORS (anyHost()),\nroutes, Ktor CIO HTTP client

== ATTESTATION FLOW — Happy Path ==

Investor -> WAF : Request compliance attestation\n(investment or redemption)

note right of WAF #FFCCCC
  **OPEN_ATTESTATION_ORACLE_ABUSE**
  Gateway has NO inbound auth.
  If WAF is bypassed, attacker
  can request attestations for
  any Approve'd address.
end note

WAF -> Ktor : Forward (after auth + rate-limit)
activate Ktor

Ktor -> Ktor : Investor validation\n(auth investor matches\ncompliance request)

' note over Ktor, HN #FFCCCC
'   **SCREENING_VERDICT_TAMPERING**
'   DNS hijack, cert injection, or
'   HYPERNATIVE_BASE_URL tampering
'   can forge an "Approve" verdict.
' end note

Ktor -> HN : Screen investor wallet address
activate HN

alt Hypernative unreachable / non-2xx / decode failure

  note over Ktor, HN #FFE0E0
    **HYPERNATIVE_OUTAGE_DOS**
    Fail-closed by design: no attestation
    issued. All investment / redemption flows
    halt until reachability restored.
  end note

  HN --> Ktor : Error / timeout / malformed

  note over Ktor #FFCCCC
    **VERBOSE_ERROR_PII_LEAK**
    502 echoes upstream request body,
    response body, headers to caller.
    Leaks Hypernative internals + investor
    address correlation.
  end note

  Ktor --> WAF : 502 Bad Gateway\n(verbose error in non-prod)
  WAF --> Investor : 502

else recommendation != "Approve"

  HN --> Ktor : Deny (+ severity, flags)
  deactivate HN
  Ktor -> Ktor : Log blocked request
  Ktor --> WAF : 403 Forbidden
  WAF --> Investor : 403

else recommendation == "Approve"

  HN --> Ktor : Approve
  deactivate HN

  note over Ktor #FFE0E0
    **COMPLIANCE_DECISION_REPUDIATION**
    Hypernative verdict is NOT durably persisted.
    After-the-fact audits cannot reconstruct
    why a given attestation was issued.
  end note

  Ktor -> Signer : Sign compliance attestation
  activate Signer

  Signer -> Signer : Build canonical message:\n"CORDA_COMPLIANCE_ATTESTATION_V1" (31B)\n++ programId(32) ++ vault(32)\n++ investor(32) ++ action(1)\n++ amount_LE(8) ++ requestId_LE(8)\n++ expiresAt_LE(8) ++ nonce(32, CSPRNG)

  note over Signer
    **Countermeasure: CANONICAL_DOMAIN_TAGGED_MESSAGE**
    Fixed-layout, domain-tagged, no varints.
    Defeats ATTESTATION_BINDING_MALLEABILITY.
  end note

  Signer -> Signer : Ed25519.sign(message)\nwith in-memory private key
  Signer --> Ktor : Signed attestation\n(message + signature + pubkey)
  deactivate Signer

  Ktor --> WAF : 200 OK — signed attestation
  deactivate Ktor
  WAF --> Investor : Signed attestation

  == ON-CHAIN VERIFICATION ==

'   note over Investor, Vault #FFCCCC
'     **ATTESTATION_REPLAY_WITHIN_TTL**
'     Attestation observable in browser memory /
'     telemetry / malicious extension. Replayable
'     for 300 s TTL. Replay safety depends on
'     vault request_id state machine.
'   end note

  Investor -> Vault : Solana Tx:\n[ Ed25519SigVerify ix\n  (msg, sig, pubkey),\n  vault.invest(\n  amount, requestId,\n  attestation { expiresAt, nonce }) ]
  activate Vault

  Vault -> Vault : require expiresAt >= clock.now
  Vault -> Vault : Rebuild expected message from\ntx args (programId, vault account,\ninvestor account, action byte,\namount, requestId, expiresAt, nonce)

  note over Vault
    **Countermeasure: ON_CHAIN_MESSAGE_RECONSTRUCTION**
    Vault rebuilds canonical message from its own
    instruction inputs. Any parameter divergence
    between signed msg and actual tx → reject.
  end note

  Vault -> Vault : Load Ed25519 sigverify ix\nfrom instructions sysvar
  Vault -> Vault : require sigverify.pubkey\n  == vault.compliance_authority
  Vault -> Vault : require sigverify.message\n  == expected_message

  alt Verification fails
    Vault --> Investor : Tx failure
  else Verification passes
    Vault -> Vault : Consume request_id\n(single-use state machine)
    Vault --> Investor : Tx success
  end
  deactivate Vault

end

== LEGACY FORWARDER (out of standard UI flow) ==

note over Ktor #FFCCCC
  **LEGACY_FORWARDER_INTERNAL_PROBE**
  /api/investment, /api/redemption forward
  raw body to VAULT_BASE_URL. If env var
  is tampered → internal network probe.
  No in-repo consumer exists.
end note

@enduml